From 7df21546ee44a932de63351875610a7bc266fb09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:37:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix security issues and missing asset build step

- Remove unauthenticated /test-data route that leaked all academies,
  branches, and users to anyone
- Fix cross-tenant IDOR in PrintController::fee() - a logged-in user
  from one academy could view/download another academy's fee receipt
  by ID
- Add defense-in-depth tenant ownership check in BaseAcademyResource
  canEdit()/canDelete() so record-level access doesn't rely solely on
  each resource remembering to scope getEloquentQuery()
- Add npm ci && npm run build (+ php artisan filament:assets) to
  deploy.sh and update.sh - this was missing entirely, which is why
  public/build never gets generated on the server and the UI renders
  unstyled/distorted
- Align composer.json license and README badge with the proprietary
  licensing already stated in the README (previously said MIT and
  linked to a LICENSE file that doesn't exist)
